[31m-- **Falsifiable Criteria**: Never use unfalsifiable goals ("utterly perfect", "complete refactor"). Define tasks with binary scoreable criteria (e.g. passing test counts, 0 lint errors, explicit hard-fails).[m
[31m-- **Carry Evidence with Claims**: "It works" means pasting terminal verification output to the PR. Exit code 0 alone proves only process survival; inspect outputs/artifacts to prove function.[m
